; worldnew.eval — a world of its own (W7).
;
; A world IS a project folder: its own overworld, dungeons, levels and content.
; This makes one and reads back what it contains. It does NOT open it — `worlds
; load` RELAUNCHES the game, which would end the run mid-script; opening one is
; the `-project <name>` flag's job, and tools/WorldTest.py drives that as a
; second run.
;
; The scratch world is removed by WorldTest's cleanup, not here.
logecho on
reset
worlds
worlds new wt_scratch
worlds
